e error message to \"gin: response body already written\", since that is now the only case that triggers it.\n- I added a test case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` for \"hijack after header write should succeed\". `go test ./...` passes.\n\nHijacking is now allowed after headers have been sent, but nothing tells the caller those headers are already on the connection. The changes are not committed (you're on a detached HEAD).","ttft_ms":3913,"type":"result","duration_ms":21804,"uuid":"80d166f7-b5a4-4b0b-961c-e0810ca0081d","ttft_stream_ms":1098,"time_to_request_ms":170,"first_content_frame_ms":1098,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
